No, in RRT, we sample nodes incrementally.

39:27.020 --> 39:31.740
So we don't have, like in the standard pathfinding setup,

39:31.740 --> 39:34.100
you're given end nodes, and you try to find the best

39:34.100 --> 39:35.780
way to explore all of them.

39:35.780 --> 39:38.180
