39:41.500 --> 39:42.380
Does that make sense?

39:42.380 --> 39:45.140
So basically, we sample a node here, we extend.

39:45.140 --> 39:47.900
We sample another node here, we extend.

39:47.900 --> 39:52.940
Actually, this question brings to an interpretation of RRT

39:52.940 --> 39:57.980
that is useful to understand what works better in practice,

39:57.980 --> 40:01.180
which is the notion of Voronoi bias.

40:01.180 --> 40:04.180
So the reason why RRT works well,

40:04.180 --> 40:07.820
and it's called rapidly exploring random tree,

40:07.820 --> 40:12.100
is that consider the vertices of the tree.

40:12.100 --> 40:15.260
And consider the Voronoi diagram with respect

40:15.260 --> 40:17.220
to the vertices of the tree.

40:17.220 --> 40:19.660
A Voronoi diagram is basically a diagram

40:19.660 --> 40:23.540
whereby you have partitioned environment into cells

40:23.540 --> 40:29.460
with a property that within each cell, each point in that cell

40:29.460 --> 40:32.980
is closer to the representative node of that cell

40:32.980 --> 40:34.460
than to any other node.

40:34.460 --> 40:37.740
So for example, here, this point is closest to this point

40:37.740 --> 40:40.580
than to this point.

40:40.580 --> 40:43.580
The boundary is the set of points

40:43.580 --> 40:47.300
that is equidistant from these two nodes.

40:47.300 --> 40:50.380
The Voronoi bias tells the following,

40:50.380 --> 40:55.020
that at the frontier of the tree,

40:55.020 --> 40:58.300
the Voronoi cells tend to be larger,

40:58.300 --> 41:02.020
which means that the likelihood that you sample in this region

41:02.020 --> 41:04.460
is larger.

41:04.460 --> 41:08.540
The likelihood of sampling is proportional to the area

41:08.540 --> 41:10.900
of the corresponding cell, which

41:10.900 --> 41:14.820
means that basically there is a strong bias in the sampling

41:14.820 --> 41:19.260
procedure towards sampling in unexplored regions.

41:19.260 --> 41:22.460
So this is basically, going back to your question,

41:22.460 --> 41:26.100
is related in a way to greedy search on an implicit graph.

41:26.100 --> 41:30.820
Implicit because we still have to sample the graph.

41:30.820 --> 41:32.980
So it's just one interpretation of why RRT is called

41:32.980 --> 41:34.260
rapidly exploring random trees.

41:38.540 --> 41:42.980
In practice, for high dimensions,

41:42.980 --> 41:47.580
it's pretty tractable to compute the full Voronoi diagram.

